   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Wow! That is embarrassing. I cannot figure out how I could miss that function. In my initial googling I actually found several other users with similar issues and I also thought I had read all of the articles on Shiny. My search strings must have been way off.<div><br></div><div>Thank you for your help and sorry for the inconvenience.</div><div><br></div><div>Morten</div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "2-PY6KjsCgAJ",
   "from": "Homer White",
   "author": "33dc9c6d026ee296",
   "date": "2016-01-04T13:58:26Z",
   "subject": "Re: Best way to validate user input and missing values",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Believe me, I have embarassed myself even worse with Shiny!</div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><br><br>On Monday, January 4, 2016 at 8:46:35 AM UTC-5, Morten Joergensen wrote:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Wow! That is embarrassing. I cannot figure out how I could miss that function. In my initial googling I actually found several other users with similar issues and I also thought I had read all of the articles on Shiny. My search strings must have been way off.<div><br></div><div>Thank you for your help and sorry for the inconvenience.</div><div><br></div><div>Morten</div></div></blockquote></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "pAbdDKX4CgAJ",
   "from": "Joe Cheng",
   "author": "ca443e6eaa0e78ed",
   "date": "2016-01-04T17:38:03Z",
   "subject": "Re: Best way to validate user input and missing values",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">validate(need(...)) is definitely intended for this. We&#39;ve also recently added a streamlined version called &quot;req&quot;, where req(x) is equivalent to calling validate(need(x, message = FALSE)). (You would still use validate/need if you want to show a message when x is missing. But it turns out you don&#39;t want to show a message in 95% of cases.)<div><br></div><div><a href=\"https://github.com/rstudio/shiny/blob/master/man/req.Rd\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/rstudio/shiny/blob/master/man/req.Rd&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792395584855000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0ZNpg4qERN1LmaKz-sY5gZ\">https://github.com/rstudio/shiny/blob/master/man/req.Rd</a><br></div><div><br></div><div>I&#39;ve rewritten your original example to use a reactive expression instead of reactive value:</div><div><br></div><div>shinyServer(function(input, output, session) {</div><div><br></div><div>  value &lt;- reactive({</div><div>    req(input$value)</div><div>    max(input$value, 0)</div><div>  })</div><div><br></div><div>  observe({</div><div>    updateNumericInput(session, &quot;value&quot;, value())</div><div>  })</div><div><br></div><div>  output$result &lt;- renderText({</div><div>    sqrt(value())</div><div>  })</div><div>})</div></div><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div dir=\"ltr\">On Mon, Jan 4, 2016 at 5:58 AM Homer White &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">homerh...@gmail.com</a>&gt; wrote:<br></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Believe me, I have embarassed myself even worse with Shiny!</div><div dir=\"ltr\"><br><br>On Monday, January 4, 2016 at 8:46:35 AM UTC-5, Morten Joergensen wrote:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Wow! That is embarrassing. I cannot figure out how I could miss that function. In my initial googling I actually found several other users with similar issues and I also thought I had read all of the articles on Shiny. My search strings must have been way off.<div><br></div><div>Thank you for your help and sorry for the inconvenience.</div><div><br></div><div>Morten</div></div></blockquote></div>\r\n\r\n<p></p></blockquote></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\">\r\n\r\n-- <br>\r\nYou received this message because you are subscribed to the Google Groups &quot;Shiny - Web Framework for R&quot; group.<br>\r\nTo unsubscribe from this group and stop receiving emails from it, send an email to <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">shiny-discus...@googlegroups.com</a>.<br>\r\nTo view this discussion on the web visit <a href=\"https://groups.google.com/d/msgid/shiny-discuss/1bf21459-0236-4e31-a0af-5983383213fb%40googlegroups.com?utm_medium=email&amp;utm_source=footer\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/d/msgid/shiny-discuss/1bf21459-0236-4e31-a0af-5983383213fb%2540googlegroups.com?utm_medium%3Demail%26utm_source%3Dfooter&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792395584855000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2ctkSJwhbPt220BMd-pPVl\">https://groups.google.com/d/msgid/shiny-discuss/1bf21459-0236-4e31-a0af-5983383213fb%40googlegroups.com</a>.<br>\r\nFor more options, visit <a href=\"https://groups.google.com/d/optout\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/d/optout&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792395584855000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2GIEMTweVoMwm7KqwJyOlw\">https://groups.google.com/d/optout</a>.<br>\r\n</blockquote></div>\r\n"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "qOpm9s8ICwAJ",
   "from": "Morten Joergensen",
   "author": "a0dd463383e0a7ff",
   "date": "2016-01-04T22:34:20Z",
   "subject": "Re: Best way to validate user input and missing values",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Thats very handy and makes the code much more readable. My check for missing input is now one simple line<div><br></div><div><div style=\"border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);word-wrap:break-word;background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\"><code><div><font color=\"#660066\"><span style=\"color:#000\">req</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(!</span><span style=\"color:#000\">any</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#008\">is</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">na</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">reactiveValuesToList</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">input</span><span style=\"color:#660\">))))</span></font><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span></div></code></div></div><div><br></div><div>Thanks.<div><br></div><div>Morten</div></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "_ClyHioKCwAJ",
   "from": "Joe Cheng",
   "author": "ca443e6eaa0e78ed",
   "date": "2016-01-04T22:59:07Z",
   "subject": "Re: Best way to validate user input and missing values",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">The only problem with reactiveValuesToList is that whoever&#39;s calling that is taking a reactive dependency on EVERY input.<div><br></div><div>Also I don&#39;t know if it was clear, but in my example I only called req() from the reactive, not from the outputs. That&#39;s because if the req() call fails in the reactive, it will stop processing not only itself but whoever called it--it&#39;s implemented as a special kind of error. In other words:</div><div><br></div><div>a &lt;- function(x) {</div><div>  req(x)</div><div>  print(&quot;a&quot;)</div><div>}</div><div><br></div><div>b &lt;- function(x) {</div><div>  a(x)</div><div>  print(&quot;b&quot;)</div><div>}</div><div><br></div><div>b(1) # prints both &quot;a&quot; and &quot;b&quot;</div><div>b(NULL) # prints nothing, errors</div></div><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div dir=\"ltr\">On Mon, Jan 4, 2016 at 2:34 PM Morten Joergensen &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">morten.joer...@gmail.com</a>&gt; wrote:<br></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Thats very handy and makes the code much more readable. My check for missing input is now one simple line<div><br></div><div><div style=\"border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);word-wrap:break-word;background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\"><code><div><font color=\"#660066\"><span style=\"color:#000\">req</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(!</span><span style=\"color:#000\">any</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#008\">is</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">na</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">reactiveValuesToList</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">input</span><span style=\"color:#660\">))))</span></font><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span></div></code></div></div><div><br></div><div>Thanks.<div><br></div><div>Morten</div></div></div>\r\n\r\n<p></p></blockquote></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\">\r\n\r\n-- <br></blockquote></div>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "<div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\">\r\nYou received this message because you are subscribed to the Google Groups &quot;Shiny - Web Framework for R&quot; group.<br>\r\nTo unsubscribe from this group and stop receiving emails from it, send an email to <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">shiny-discus...@googlegroups.com</a>.<br></blockquote></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\">\r\nTo view this discussion on the web visit <a href=\"https://groups.google.com/d/msgid/shiny-discuss/632f8dcd-089a-4e5e-9467-19b699a9511e%40googlegroups.com?utm_medium=email&amp;utm_source=footer\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/d/msgid/shiny-discuss/632f8dcd-089a-4e5e-9467-19b699a9511e%2540googlegroups.com?utm_medium%3Demail%26utm_source%3Dfooter&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792395584857000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tG40lwWSf6ObiKXq9bQVC\">https://groups.google.com/d/msgid/shiny-discuss/632f8dcd-089a-4e5e-9467-19b699a9511e%40googlegroups.com</a>.</blockquote></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><br>\r\nFor more options, visit <a href=\"https://groups.google.com/d/optout\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/d/optout&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792395584857000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2MY5G3YkTnhnH_rpxZy213\">https://groups.google.com/d/optout</a>.<br>\r\n</blockquote></div>"
