  {
   "id": "8sSIzskmCwAJ",
   "from": "Morten Joergensen",
   "author": "a0dd463383e0a7ff",
   "date": "2016-01-05T07:43:39Z",
   "subject": "Re: Best way to validate user input and missing values",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Yes, thanks for the clarification. The code was intended to stop everything if any input was missing but it might be better to specify the input variables. I very much like that the req (and validate) can trace back dependencies and stop them - it makes it very powerfull.<div><br></div><div>Morten</div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "82oxlIwYDAAJ",
   "from": "Morten Joergensen",
   "author": "a0dd463383e0a7ff",
   "date": "2016-01-08T09:33:57Z",
   "subject": "Re: Best way to validate user input and missing values",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Just wanted to share if anyone comes by this thread:<div><br></div><div>It seems that ggvis (which I use in many of my apps) does not play along nicely with validate/req. It works somehow if ggvis is wrapped in a reactive/observe and the reactive data function (with parentheses) is passed to ggvis i.e.</div><div><br></div><div><div style=\"border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);word-wrap:break-word;background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\"><code><div><div style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><span style=\"color:#000\">observe</span><span style=\"color:#660\">({</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  data</span><span style=\"color:#660\">()</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">%&gt;%</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    ggvis</span><span style=\"color:#660\">()%&gt;%</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>     bind_shiny</span><span style=\"color:#660\">()</span></div><div style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><span style=\"color:#660\">)}</span></div></div></code></div><br>This may cause some inefficient renderings of the plot though</div><div><br></div><div>Morten</div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  }
 ]
}
